<https://example.org/openevidence/questions/q_gastroesophageal_reflux_disease_treatment> a holon:ClinicalQuestionHolon ;
    oe:questionText "What is the recommended first-line pharmacological treatment for Gastroesophageal Reflux Disease?"^^xsd:string ;
    oe:answerText "Gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD) is caused by the reflux of gastric contents into the esophagus due to a decline in esophageal clearance and anti-reflux barrier mechanisms. Mucosal injury is caused by a combination of gastric juice directly damaging the esophageal mucosa and the immune and inflammatory mechanism in which inflammatory cytokines released from the esophageal mucosal epithelium cause neutrophil migration, triggering inflammation."^^xsd:string ;
    holon:hasInteriorGraph <https://example.org/openevidence/questions/q_gastroesophageal_reflux_disease_treatment-int> ;
    holon:hasBoundaryGraph <https://example.org/openevidence/questions/q_gastroesophageal_reflux_disease_treatment-bou> ;
    holon:hasProjectionGraph <https://example.org/openevidence/questions/q_gastroesophageal_reflux_disease_treatment-pro> ;
    holon:hasContextGraph <https://example.org/openevidence/questions/q_gastroesophageal_reflux_disease_treatment-con> .

<https://example.org/openevidence/drugs/omeprazole> oe:treats <https://example.org/openevidence/diseases/gastroesophageal_reflux_disease> .
